  "visualBrief": "Temple of Kom Ombo present-day medium-fi surviving double temple: stepped river-facing approach, broken forecourt shafts, paired entrance axes with low screens, floral-capital hypostyle columns, surviving stone lintels/cavetto cornices and winged discs, narrower inner hall, paired roofless rear shrines, mapped enclosure remnants and ancillary ruins, and a shallow visible well-mouth treatment. No complete ancient roof, intact pylon, detailed hieroglyph inventory or neighboring Crocodile Museum is reconstructed.",
