  "sourceFacts": {
    "horizontalBasis": "Q1243401/way90446374 identifies the ruin precinct rather than a solid modern building. The standard map supplies the stepped main-hall footprint, two large L-shaped enclosure strips, seven small ancillary remnants, a west detached ruin and the circular well. Internal+U runs northeast; the paired main front faces southwest toward the river. The low front, broad main hall and narrowing rear arrangement follow the mapped vertices. The Crocodile Museum and small later kiosk remain independent, with a0.1mm numerical margin at shared mask edges.",
    "architecturalHeights": "Three ordinary photographs guide the surviving form. Approximate14m upper front cornice, about10.7m floral columns, low screen walls4.6m, broken forecourt shafts1.8–4m and lower irregular rear chambers. Main10-column and smaller6-column groupings, secondary partitions and individual capitals are visualization estimates from pictures and mapped plan dimensions, not a surveyed stone inventory. Fine carved narratives and inscriptions are omitted."
  },
