    "heightBasis": "Three ordinary photographs guide the surviving form. Approximate14m upper front cornice, about10.7m floral columns, low screen walls4.6m, broken forecourt shafts1.8–4m and lower irregular rear chambers. Main10-column and smaller6-column groupings, secondary partitions and individual capitals are visualization estimates from pictures and mapped plan dimensions, not a surveyed stone inventory. Fine carved narratives and inscriptions are omitted.",
